= Energy — Simple =

'''Energy''' is a measurable feature of things that move, are heated, or can change something else. The main scientific unit is the joule.

A rolling ball has energy because it moves. A raised object has energy because of its position. A warm object has energy associated with the motion and interactions of its particles.

Energy can move between objects and change form. When a bicycle brakes, its motion energy becomes mostly heat. The energy is not destroyed.

'''Power''' means how quickly energy is transferred, while [[Energy efficiency|efficiency]] compares useful results to the energy put into a process.

